WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:03.230
Did he just call her his enemy?

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.710
Does that mean they're rivals?

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.980
Incredible! Ichijoji declared her his rival?

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.720
How long have you known each other?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.310
Actually, um...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.370
Isn't it amazing that you're in the same class?

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.300
Well...

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.160
No, they must know each other.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.290
What? That can't be right.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.290
Ichijoji never does anything like that.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.520
I was super scared.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.500
This isn't good.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.140
Wrong again.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:54.200
<b>Magic-Kyun! Renaissance</b>

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.980
Only You Can See

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.280
Kohana-san, didn't the king 
walk you to the dorms?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.360
That's why I thought you two 
already knew about each other.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.810
There's been bad blood between the 
Aigasaki and Ichijoji families

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.570
since the Muromachi period.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.070
What? Muromachi?

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.240
As in feudal times?

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.170
Yeah.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.720
One family of renowned flower arrangers, 
the other, renowned musicians.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.120
Apparently they've even 
fought over political power.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.260
Seriously?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.830
Seriously?

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.850
Most people involved in the 
magical arts know about it.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.840
Did your family ever tell you about it?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.350
No, not at all.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.230
Oh, I see.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.710
But no matter what the king says,

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:54.980
it's not your fault.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.900
Don't worry about it.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.940
Although, I know you probably will.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.320
Yeah.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.240
Today, I'll be teaching you 
a method for measuring

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.750
what you feel when you see certain colors.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:12.920
You did it.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.420
You're my enemy.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.420
Tone, taste, smell.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.430
You'll be able to understand 
how we feel these things.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.430
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.430
<b>Hoshi Festival 
House</b>

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:31.760
I'm on the executive committee 
with Ichijoji-kun.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.390
I wonder if we'll be okay.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.940
That's it. The Hoshi Festival House.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.700
Excuse me.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.710
These are photos of the Hoshi Festival.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.110
Wow. They've been doing this for a long time.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.220
Huh...

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.220
This is...

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.540
My mom was on the Hoshi Festival 
executive committee, too.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.590
Wow.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.730
The year Aigasaki Sakura 
chaired the committee,

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.440
the festival was called the Summer 
Festival of Miracles and Blessings.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.110
People still talk about it.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.680
Miracles and Blessings?

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.370
And that year, she became 
the Artista Princess.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.490
The Artista Princess?

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.240
My mom climbed those stairs?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.730
Mom...

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.500
Sir, were you a student at Hoshigei then?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.760
The conference room is this way.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.370
Yes, sir.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.390
All right. I'll do my best, too.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.850
I'll make this festival as
wonderful as my mom's was.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.520
I know I can do it.

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.400
<i>I forgot I had this wall to overcome.</i>

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.860
<i>No one's coming.</i>

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.480
Waiting any longer would be a waste of time.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.300
What?

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.380
And why did it have to be these members, sir?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.480
Who knows?

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.430
It was the principal's decision.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.680
With Suminomiya on the committee, 
we won't get anything done.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.270
We can't help what's already been decided.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.830
We're talking about Suminomiya here.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.010
In any case, you're free to go for today.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.320
No.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.820
We should change the 
members on the committee.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:45.780
What?

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.350
They didn't even come to the first meeting.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.960
Someone like that doesn't 
deserve to be on the committee.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.830
The Hoshi Festival is Hoshigei's biggest event.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.810
The executive committee is 
responsible for making everything,

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.840
including the Art Session, a success.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.910
E-Excuse me, but what's the Art Session?

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:10.340
It's a collaborative performance of various 
magical arts arranged by the executive committee.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.350
A collaboration?

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.720
We should choose new members.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.920
But I'd like to do it.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:22.980
I'll do my best.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.480
I'm not taking you off the committee.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:26.480
What?

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.990
Why would we dismiss someone
 who actually showed up?

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.430
Todo-sensei, I will choose new 
members for the committee.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.250
Wait a moment.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:41.470
M-Maybe we should reach 
out to the others again.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:44.420
There might be some reason 
they didn't attend.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.260
You do it, then.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.300
What?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.630
I know. You can start with Suminomiya Aoi.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.780
He's in our class.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.390
It'll be easier to talk to him.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.770
How naive.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.080
No matter what you say, he won't come.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.650
You don't know that until you try.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.650
It's pointless. He won't come.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.150
Then why did you tell me to start with him?

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.130
Because if you're going to get discouraged,

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.530
sooner would be better than later.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.450
I won't get discouraged.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.540
I promise I'll bring him.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.490
He's the worst!

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.560
I'll definitely bring him to the meeting.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.800
But I'm not sure you can get Suminomiya 
the Eccentric to attend a meeting.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.310
What? Wh-Why not?

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:42.650
<i>He's only come to class about five 
times since he started school.</i>

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:43.560
<i>What?</i>

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.710
<i>But what about his attendance record?</i>

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.880
<i>Oh, he's not skipping his studies.</i>

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.320
<i>He spends hours every day studying on his own.</i>

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:51.880
<i>Self-study?</i>

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:52.620
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.450
<i>They say the light of his arte 
constantly pours out of the Aoi Zone.</i>

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.950
<i>The Aoi Zone?</i>

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.250
<i>The self-study room in the east building.</i>

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.380
<i>Used by no one else,</i>

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.460
<i>it's a room of Suminomiya Aoi by 
Suminomiya Aoi for Suminomiya Aoi.</i>

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.960
<i>They call it the Aoi Zone.</i>

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.390
Oh, Aoi.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:13.970
Okay.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.720
Excuse me.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.900
This isn't right, either.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.570
<i>He's the one with the spiky sparkles.</i>

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:36.240
You...

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:37.620
Yes?

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:42.500
You have ink on your face.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:59.540
Um, I'm here regarding the Hoshi 
Festival executive committee.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.940
Oh, I'm a transfer student.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.270
I'm Aigasaki Kohana, a student in your class.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:09.550
You were chosen for the executive committee,

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:11.780
so I'd appreciate if you 
could attend the meetings.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:17.500
Suminomiya-kun?

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.780
Ichijoji told me about it.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:22.720
Yes.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:25.350
I'm not interested.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:30.980
But everyone's looking forward 
to the Hoshi Festival.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.160
I'm sure it's worth doing.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:54.570
His sparkles are so pointy.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.070
This one is spiky.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.320
Is this one thorny?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.580
They're like a rose's thorns.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.160
These are cute.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.330
They look like rock candy.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.650
Is this one pointier?

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.830
No, this one?

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.460
Is this right?

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.600
How did you know?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.550
I'm sorry. Was I not supposed to touch them?

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:29.480
No. You lined them up in the order I drew them.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.620
Oh, right.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.270
I arranged them according
 to how pointy the sparkles are.

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.700
Pointy?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:40.240
Is that how you see them?

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:47.310
Yeah. They're least pointy to 
most pointy from there to here.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:50.500
And the amount decreases little by little.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.920
That's not possible.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.660
What? B-But...

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:58.570
I should be getting closer 
to what I want to write.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.180
What you want to write?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:05.230
That's right. There's something I want to write.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:09.660
I don't know myself what that is.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:14.870
Until I find it, I'll keep on writing.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.320
I should be able to find it soon.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:22.950
I have to find it soon.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.360
You couldn't do it, could you?

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.420
I haven't given up yet.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:48.340
He's not interested in other people's affairs.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.850
He's always been that way.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:51.680
Always?

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.380
It's none of your business.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.210
Do you know something?

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.190
Just give up.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.990
I won't give up.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:07.420
Magic-Kyun for you.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.340
Magic-Kyun.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:12.420
Renaissance.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:17.460
Oh, yeah. The eccentric and the 
king are childhood friends.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.920
It's hard to believe, but they 
used to be great friends.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.100
What?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.590
But now they're rivals.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:25.340
Rivals?

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:29.850
They're candidates number one and 
two for this year's artista prince.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.820
Sometimes they switch ranks.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.270
Really?

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.180
Considering how the Eccentric acts,

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.430
he probably doesn't care at all.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.360
But I don't know about the king.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.620
Today's the day.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.910
Excuse me.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:50.410
Huh?

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:52.660
I've been waiting for you.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.810
What?

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.210
Oh, good.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.040
You've decided to come 
to the committee meeting.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.600
Huh?

00:12:58.600 --> 00:12:59.340
Well?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:00.120
What?

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.070
What do you see?

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:08.800
Um, can you not see them?

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:12.240
I can't. I could before.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.560
But now I can't.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:15.750
Well?

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.560
Well...

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.280
They're even pointier than yesterday.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.690
And there's less of them.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.450
That shouldn't be.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.950
Suminomiya-kun?

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.660
That shouldn't...

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:34.820
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.710
<b>Chocolate Roll
Monja Flavor</b>

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.710
<b>Anchovy & Vegetable Juice
Cream Puff</b>

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.580
All they had left at the store were 
monja-flavored chocolate rolls

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.910
and anchovy and vegetable juice cream puffs.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:47.060
Sorry.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.280
I guess you don't care at all.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.110
Thanks for the food.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.470
<i>Have we gotten a little closer?</i>

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.540
<i>But he's still ignoring 
the executive committee.</i>

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:18.960
This place is a mess.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.960
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:29.250
He's so focused.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.340
Okay.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:02.860
I'm finished.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.020
They're different.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.060
The paper, the ink, the color.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.640
Incredible. There are more sparkles.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.450
Their color is bright, too.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:40.850
I see.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.710
I didn't dislike the pointy sparkles.

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.880
But today's were really beautiful.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.120
I see.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.320
So will he come to the committee meetings?

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:51.880
Uh...

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.850
I forgot about that.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.220
But I'm so happy.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.860
Really?

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:18.190
So bright.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.020
This isn't right, either.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.270
<i>There are more sparkles than before.</i>

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.330
<i>But this isn't what he really wants to write.</i>

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.410
<i>Is there anything else I can do for him?</i>

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:54.900
<i>There is.</i>

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:56.780
<i>There is something.</i>

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:03.040
<i>I'll support Suminomiya-kun 
with my flower arrangements.</i>

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:09.350
<i>Like they're growing 
straight towards the sun.</i>

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:16.470
<i>Like a lot of plants coming together 
to form one beautiful flower.</i>

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.610
Done.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.740
Suminomiya-kun?

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:45.250
What a lovely and warm light.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.500
What?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.580
I see it.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.840
It's the first light I've seen 
since coming to Hoshigei.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:10.650
<b>Bright Light</b>

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.890
<i>The world I see has started shining</i>

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:29.370
<i>Because of the flowers 
blooming with your light</i>

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:33.630
<i>This time, I hope you'll 
let me gently protect them</i>

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:54.860
<i>Darkly blurred words begin to fade</i>

00:18:56.190 --> 00:19:01.610
<i>With the miracle you brought to me</i>

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:09.700
<i>Even the fragile and 
short-lived specks of light</i>

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:17.140
<i>You picked up one by one</i>

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:25.970
<i>From the shadows where I used to stay, 
before I knew it</i>

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:33.020
<i>You took me out into the sun</i>

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:36.960
<i>The world you see is warm</i>

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.530
<i>I promise you this light</i>

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.490
<i>Will become the rain and the wind</i>

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:48.750
<i>To make the flower you are bloom</i>

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.030
Amazing. This is amazing, Aoi-kun.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.580
You wrote what you wanted to write.

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:08.500
This isn't right, either.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:09.060
What?

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.040
But it's close.

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:13.360
I know I'm getting closer.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:20.530
Thank you. This is because of you.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.540
Suminomiya-kun will be 
attending starting today.

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:33.400
S-Sure.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.540
Thanks for coming.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:37.790
Sure.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:39.700
I'll make some tea.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:43.720
Thanks. Ichijoji, you're running the meeting.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:44.800
Yes, sir.

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:55.240
Wait.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:21:00.320
I didn't think you would come.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:01.800
Why did you?

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.740
I don't know.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.320
I guess because she showed me something

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:11.140
I wasn't able to see for a long time.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.330
Aigasaki did?

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.550
Yeah.

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:22.840
We used to watch the sunset 
together all the time.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.030
I've forgotten.

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.980
I'm sure I can get the others to come, too.

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.980
Tatewaki Rintaro-senpai.

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:43.740
Anjo Louis-senpai.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.240
Tsukushi Monet-kun.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.740
Hibiki Kanato-kun.

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:52.240
It's okay. I'm sure I can do it.

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.990
I must admit you did well this time.

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:30.260
You're never honest about your feelings.

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:32.510
You've become quite talkative.

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:35.300
Next time on <i>Magic-Kyun! Renaissance</i>:

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>#3 Inspiration in an Album</b>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.160
"Inspiration in an Album."

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.190
For you.

00:23:39.190 --> 00:23:39.980
Magic-Kyun.
